F292                             ; ---- the tail ---------------------------------------------------------------
F292                             ; "/" is the last handler, so what follows its first byte may lie past the
F292                             ; second range: the divide itself and the routines after it.
F292                             ; "/" ( a b -- r q ): the quotient is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
F292                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
F292                             ; of a. Dividing by zero is not checked: it returns two cells of no meaning.
